{
  "id": "x86-registers",
  "order": 10,
  "title": "The sixteen registers",
  "blurb": "Every general-purpose register on x86-64, what the calling convention does with it, and who has to restore it.",
  "note": "The names are inherited from the 8086 and almost none of them still means what it says. What is real is the column about who saves it, because that is a contract nothing in the processor enforces.",
  "checked": "2026-09-01",
  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "System V Application Binary Interface, AMD64 Processor Supplement",
      "url": "https://gitlab.com/x86-psABIs/x86-64-ABI"
    }
  ],
  "columns": [
